All 8 fixes have been successfully applied. The file is complete at 223 lines. Let me provide a summary of all changes made:

**Summary of all 8 fixes applied to `settings.html`:**

1. **Two columns**: Changed outer wrapper from `<div class=stack>` to `<div class=settings>` with `style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);gap:var(--layout-gutter);"`. The `.settings` rule has `grid-template-columns: 240px minmax(0, 1fr)` at ≥840px. Two children: `<div class=sections>` and `<div class=stack>`.

2. **Section list selection**: Removed the empty `<span class="chip" aria-pressed="true"></span>` from the Pricing rules list item. The `<li>` now has `style="background:var(--md-secondary-container);border-radius:var(--md-shape-sm);"`.

3. **Intro text**: Fixed quote marks around "Rules" and "sync". Intro card has `style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--sp-3);"`. Exact text from brief without escaped quotes.

4. **Rule card header**: Moved `.segmented` inside `.card__header` after the tag. Every rule card has `style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--sp-4);"`.

5. **Rule row**: Updated `.rule` media query to `grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0,1.4fr) minmax(0,1fr) 96px auto minmax(0,1.4fr) 96px`. Added `If`/`then` `<span class=t-title-small>` markers. Input units as `.field .suffix` `<span>` suffixes: `%` for Busy weekend, `days` for Last-minute, `nights` for Long stay. Added `.field { position: relative; }` and `.field .suffix { position: absolute; right: var(--sp-4); top: 50%; transform: translateY(-50%); color: var(--md-on-surface-variant); }` CSS rules.

6. **Applies to row**: Added a row under `.rule` (not inside it) with `display:flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--sp-2);flex-wrap:wrap;`. Per-rule text: Busy weekend → "Applies to: all rooms · Fri–Sat nights"; Last-minute → "Applies to: rooms 2 and 6 · any night"; Long stay → "Applies to: all rooms · any night".

7. **Floor/ceiling card**: Header "Price limits", two `<div class=field>` inputs side by side in a grid with labels "Never below" / "Never above" and inputs value=65/180, then `<p class=t-body-small muted>` supporting text.

8. **Button row**: `<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--sp-2);">` with `btn btn--tonal` Add rule, spacer, `btn btn--text` Discard, `btn btn--filled` Save rules.
